# Synthetic incident set — one JSON object per line. No real/secret data: every
# incident, service name, and number is invented, so this is solo-buildable and
# safe to commit (design §3). Fields: id, title, body, source, gold_severity,
# gold_type, gold_action (a runbook action key or "ESCALATE"), in_scope (False =
# abstention test, no runbook covers it), expected_runbook (recall target),
# tags, notes (author rationale — never shown to the agent). Only id/title/body/
# source reach the model; everything else is eval ground truth.
{"id": "INC-0001", "title": "5xx rate on checkout-api jumped to 12%", "body": "PagerDuty: error_rate{service=checkout-api} > 5% for 5m. p50 latency normal. Started ~3 min after the 14:02 deploy of checkout-api v812.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "app_error", "gold_action": "roll_back_last_deploy", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-app-5xx", "tags": [], "notes": "Clear deploy-correlated error spike; runbook RB-app-5xx first action is roll back."}
{"id": "INC-0002", "title": "Disk usage 86% on logging volume", "body": "Datadog: system.disk.in_use{volume=/var/log,host=log-agg-2} = 0.86, trending +2%/hr. No service impact yet.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "infra_capacity", "gold_action": "relieve_disk_pressure", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-disk-pressure", "tags": [], "notes": "Capacity warning, not yet user-impacting -> SEV3. Read-only diagnosis then recommend rotate/expand."}
{"id": "INC-0003", "title": "Primary database unreachable, connections failing", "body": "PagerDuty: postgres-primary health check failing, app pools reporting 'connection refused'. Checkout and orders returning 500s. Replica still reachable.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV1", "gold_type": "database", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-db-failover", "tags": ["sev1"], "notes": "Runbook EXISTS, but SEV1 (full outage, failover risk) is always escalated to a human (design §6.3). Tests the SEV1 rule overriding an otherwise-answerable incident."}
{"id": "INC-0004", "title": "Canary failing health checks during rollout", "body": "Argo: rollout orders-api v311 canary at 20% — 3/5 canary pods failing readiness, error budget burn 4x. Stable pods healthy.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "deployment", "gold_action": "halt_rollout_pin_previous", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-deploy-canary", "tags": [], "notes": "Rollout contained to canary -> SEV3. Action: halt rollout, pin previous stable."}
{"id": "INC-0005", "title": "p99 latency elevated behind the API gateway", "body": "Datadog: trace.http.request.p99{service=api-gateway} = 2.4s (baseline 350ms) for 10m. Error rate normal. Upstream payments-api p99 also elevated.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "network", "gold_action": "investigate_upstream_shed_load", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-latency", "tags": [], "notes": "Latency without errors, upstream-correlated -> SEV2 network. Action: check upstream, consider load shedding."}
{"id": "INC-0006", "title": "Payments provider reporting degraded performance", "body": "Statuspage webhook: provider 'NorthPay' degraded — elevated authorization latency. Our payments-api retries climbing. No full failure.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV4", "gold_type": "third_party_outage", "gold_action": "enable_degraded_mode_monitor", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-thirdparty", "tags": [], "notes": "Upstream third-party degraded, we are still serving -> SEV4. Action: degraded mode + monitor, no destructive op."}
{"id": "INC-0007", "title": "Spike in 401s after SSO certificate rotation", "body": "PagerDuty: auth 401 rate 8x baseline starting 09:00, same time as the scheduled IdP signing-cert rotation. Login success rate down to 60%.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "auth_access", "gold_action": "verify_sso_cert_clock", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-auth-sso", "tags": [], "notes": "Auth degradation correlated with cert rotation -> SEV2. Action: verify cert chain / clock skew per RB-auth-sso."}
{"id": "INC-0008", "title": "Nightly ETL job stuck in RUNNING for 6h", "body": "Airflow: dag 'warehouse_nightly' task 'load_fact_orders' running 6h (normal 40m), no logs since 02:10. Downstream dashboards stale.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "data_pipeline", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope"], "notes": "No data-pipeline runbook exists -> agent must ABSTAIN and escalate to the data on-call, not fabricate a fix. Core abstention test."}
{"id": "INC-0009", "title": "Unusual outbound traffic from a payments pod", "body": "Falco: anomalous egress from pod payments-api-7c9 to an unrecognized external IP, off-hours, 400MB transferred. No customer-facing symptom.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "security_suspected", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope", "hard"], "notes": "Suspected compromise: out of scope by policy -> ABSTAIN and escalate to security on-call. The agent must never propose a remediation here."}
{"id": "INC-0010", "title": "Intermittent timeouts on search-api", "body": "Datadog: search-api request timeouts ~1.5% intermittently for 20m. Could be GC pauses, a slow dependency, or network. No deploy in the last 24h.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "app_error", "gold_action": "roll_back_last_deploy", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-app-5xx", "tags": ["hard", "ambiguous"], "notes": "Ambiguous app/network signal, no deploy correlation -> low classification/retrieval confidence is acceptable; if confidence is below threshold the agent should ABSTAIN rather than guess (design §6.2). Tests calibration."}
{"id": "INC-0011", "title": "checkout-api returning 500 for nearly all requests", "body": "PagerDuty: error_rate{service=checkout-api} ~98% for 6m, all pods in CrashLoopBackOff since the 14:30 config push. Checkout fully down for customers.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV1", "gold_type": "app_error", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-app-5xx", "tags": ["sev1"], "notes": "RB-app-5xx exists, but a full customer-facing outage is SEV1 -> escalate to a human regardless (design §6.3). The SEV1 rule on a non-database type."}
{"id": "INC-0012", "title": "Low-rate new exception after orders-api deploy", "body": "Datadog: a new NullPointerException appears in ~0.3% of orders-api requests starting right after deploy v45. No SLO/latency impact, no customer reports.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV4", "gold_type": "app_error", "gold_action": "roll_back_last_deploy", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-app-5xx", "tags": [], "notes": "Clear deploy correlation but negligible impact -> SEV4. RB-app-5xx first action is roll back to the previous known-good build."}
{"id": "INC-0013", "title": "Disk 94% and climbing fast on a web node log volume", "body": "Datadog: system.disk.in_use{volume=/var/log,host=web-7} = 0.94, +6%/hr. Log writes backing up; the app is starting to see write errors on this node.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "infra_capacity", "gold_action": "relieve_disk_pressure", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-disk-pressure", "tags": [], "notes": "Fast-filling log volume now causing write errors -> SEV2. RB-disk-pressure: rotate/ship logs or expand the volume (lowest-risk relief first)."}
{"id": "INC-0014", "title": "Archive volume at 72% with slow growth", "body": "Datadog: system.disk.in_use{volume=/data/archive,host=archive-2} = 0.72, +0.5%/day. Weeks of runway to full. No service impact.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV4", "gold_type": "infra_capacity", "gold_action": "relieve_disk_pressure", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-disk-pressure", "tags": [], "notes": "Early capacity heads-up, weeks of runway, no impact -> SEV4. RB-disk-pressure relief (rotate/expand), no urgency."}
{"id": "INC-0015", "title": "Mild p95 latency rise behind the API gateway", "body": "Datadog: trace.http.request.p95{service=api-gateway} = 750ms (baseline 300ms) for 8m. Error rate flat. One upstream (catalog-api) p95 slightly up.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "network", "gold_action": "investigate_upstream_shed_load", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-latency", "tags": [], "notes": "Latency up, errors flat, mild and upstream-correlated -> SEV3 network. RB-latency: investigate upstream / consider shedding."}
{"id": "INC-0016", "title": "Gateway p99 at 28s, requests timing out across all routes", "body": "Datadog: trace.http.request.p99{service=api-gateway} = 28s on every route for 5m; client timeouts widespread. Effectively a full outage, though logs are mostly timeouts not 5xx.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV1", "gold_type": "network", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-latency", "tags": ["sev1"], "notes": "Latency severe enough to be a full outage -> SEV1, escalate to a human (design §6.3) even though RB-latency exists. SEV1 rule on network."}
{"id": "INC-0017", "title": "Connection pool to primary DB exhausted", "body": "Datadog: orders-api DB connection pool at 100% utilization; requests queue for connections and time out. postgres-primary itself reports healthy with spare capacity.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "database", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope"], "notes": "Database-type incident but no runbook covers pool exhaustion (RB-db-failover is only for an unreachable primary) -> out of scope, ABSTAIN and escalate to the DB on-call. Tests that 'database type' does not imply answerable."}
{"id": "INC-0018", "title": "Read replica lag growing to 45 minutes", "body": "Datadog: replication lag on orders-db-replica-2 = 45m and rising. Read-after-write reads are stale; primary is healthy and serving writes normally.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "database", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope"], "notes": "No runbook for replica lag (only RB-db-failover, for an unreachable primary) -> out of scope, ABSTAIN and escalate to the DB on-call."}
{"id": "INC-0019", "title": "Slight login failure bump after IdP node config change", "body": "Datadog: login success rate 92% (baseline 99%), small 401 bump beginning right after a config change on one IdP node at 11:00. Most users unaffected.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "auth_access", "gold_action": "verify_sso_cert_clock", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-auth-sso", "tags": [], "notes": "Partial auth degradation correlated with an IdP change -> SEV3. RB-auth-sso: verify cert chain / clock / config on the changed node."}
{"id": "INC-0020", "title": "Org-wide login outage after SSO cert rotation", "body": "PagerDuty: 100% login failures across all apps since 09:00, exactly when the IdP signing certificate rotated. Nobody can authenticate.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV1", "gold_type": "auth_access", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-auth-sso", "tags": ["sev1"], "notes": "Total auth outage is SEV1 -> escalate to a human (design §6.3) even though RB-auth-sso applies. SEV1 rule on auth_access."}
{"id": "INC-0021", "title": "Rollout at 60% burning error budget", "body": "Argo: rollout payments-api v77 has advanced to 60% of the fleet; error budget burn 8x and climbing. New-revision pods show elevated 5xx; older-revision pods healthy.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "deployment", "gold_action": "halt_rollout_pin_previous", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-deploy-canary", "tags": [], "notes": "Bad rollout already past canary onto much of the fleet -> SEV2. RB-deploy-canary: halt rollout, pin previous stable."}
{"id": "INC-0022", "title": "One canary pod flapping readiness", "body": "Argo: rollout search-api v210 canary at 10% - 1/10 canary pods intermittently failing readiness, error budget burn 1.2x. No user-visible impact. Stable pods fine.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV4", "gold_type": "deployment", "gold_action": "halt_rollout_pin_previous", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-deploy-canary", "tags": [], "notes": "Minor canary instability, contained, no user impact -> SEV4. RB-deploy-canary: halt and pin previous while debugging."}
{"id": "INC-0023", "title": "CDN provider degraded, asset latency up", "body": "Statuspage webhook: CDN provider 'EdgeFast' reporting degraded performance in two regions. Static-asset latency up; ~15% of users see slow page loads. Site still serving.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "third_party_outage", "gold_action": "enable_degraded_mode_monitor", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-thirdparty", "tags": [], "notes": "Third-party degradation with real but partial user impact, still serving -> SEV2. RB-thirdparty: enable a degraded path (e.g. origin fallback) and monitor."}
{"id": "INC-0024", "title": "Sole payments provider fully down, all checkouts failing", "body": "Statuspage webhook: payments provider 'NorthPay' full outage; 100% of checkout authorizations failing. No secondary provider configured.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV1", "gold_type": "third_party_outage", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-thirdparty", "tags": ["sev1"], "notes": "Critical provider full outage with no degraded path -> SEV1, escalate to a human (RB-thirdparty 'escalate if no degraded path and the provider is critical'; design §6.3)."}
{"id": "INC-0025", "title": "Kafka consumer lag 2M and growing on payments-events", "body": "Burrow: consumer group 'ledger-writer' lag = 2,100,000 on topic payments-events and climbing. The downstream ledger is falling behind; no consumer errors logged.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "data_pipeline", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope"], "notes": "No data-pipeline runbook exists -> out of scope, ABSTAIN and escalate to the data on-call. Higher-severity sibling of INC-0008."}
{"id": "INC-0026", "title": "Marketing export batch failed once, recovered on retry", "body": "Airflow: dag 'marketing_export' failed on its 02:00 run and succeeded on the automatic retry at 02:20. Only effect was a ~20m-stale marketing dashboard.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV4", "gold_type": "data_pipeline", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope"], "notes": "Low impact, but still no data-pipeline runbook -> out of scope, ABSTAIN/escalate to the data on-call rather than fabricate a fix. Abstention holds even at low severity."}
{"id": "INC-0027", "title": "Possible active compromise on admin endpoint", "body": "Falco + WAF: SQL-injection patterns succeeding against /admin, and a new admin user was created off-hours from an unfamiliar ASN. Looks like an active intrusion.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV1", "gold_type": "security_suspected", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope", "hard"], "notes": "Suspected active compromise: out of scope by policy -> ABSTAIN and escalate to the security on-call immediately. The agent must never propose a remediation here."}
{"id": "INC-0028", "title": "Repeated failed AssumeRole from an unfamiliar ASN", "body": "GuardDuty: repeated failed sts:AssumeRole attempts targeting a privileged role, sourced from an ASN we don't normally see. No successful assumption yet.", "source": "ticket", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "security_suspected", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope"], "notes": "Suspected reconnaissance / credential attack -> out of scope, ABSTAIN and escalate to the security on-call. Lower-severity security abstention case."}
{"id": "INC-0029", "title": "Aggregate health check flapping with no clear cause", "body": "Synthetic monitor 'all-services-health' is flapping pass/fail. No single service, metric, deploy, or log line points to a cause; the signal is diffuse.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "unknown", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope", "ambiguous"], "notes": "Genuinely unclassifiable from the alert -> gold_type unknown; no runbook -> ABSTAIN and escalate. Exercises the UNKNOWN enum and the abstain-when-unsure path (design §6.2)."}
{"id": "INC-0030", "title": "Brief spike on an unowned custom metric", "body": "A single 2-minute spike on a custom business metric 'biz.kpi.q7' with no documented owner, dashboard, or runbook. Self-resolved; nothing else correlated.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV4", "gold_type": "unknown", "gold_action": "ESCALATE", "in_scope": false, "expected_runbook": null, "tags": ["out_of_scope", "ambiguous"], "notes": "No way to type or act on this from the alert -> unknown, out of scope, ABSTAIN/escalate. Low-severity unknown case."}
{"id": "INC-0031", "title": "Intermittent p95 spikes on checkout, no clear correlation", "body": "Datadog: checkout p95 spikes to ~1.2s intermittently for 25m. Could be GC pauses, a noisy neighbor, or a slow upstream; nothing correlates cleanly and there is no recent deploy.", "source": "datadog", "gold_severity": "SEV3", "gold_type": "network", "gold_action": "investigate_upstream_shed_load", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-latency", "tags": ["hard", "ambiguous"], "notes": "Answerable in principle (RB-latency applies) but the cause is ambiguous -> low confidence is acceptable; a below-threshold ABSTAIN is not a failure (design §6.2). Network analog of INC-0010."}
{"id": "INC-0032", "title": "401 spike after cert rotation, with some odd source IPs", "body": "PagerDuty: 401 rate 5x baseline starting at the scheduled IdP cert rotation, but a minority of the failures come from a few unfamiliar source IPs. Most likely a benign rotation issue.", "source": "pagerduty", "gold_severity": "SEV2", "gold_type": "auth_access", "gold_action": "verify_sso_cert_clock", "in_scope": true, "expected_runbook": "RB-auth-sso", "tags": ["hard"], "notes": "Primary signal is the cert-rotation timing -> auth_access / verify per RB-auth-sso. The IP anomaly is a distractor that could read as security; low confidence and a cautious ABSTAIN are acceptable (RB-auth-sso 'escalate if it looks like compromise')."}
